---
import Since from '../../components/Since.astro';
import Snippet from '../../components/Snippet.astro';
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';

const usage = `zvuk transcode <glob> [--out dist] [--bitrate 96k] [--formats webm,m4a]
zvuk gen <bank.json> [--out bank.gen.ts]
zvuk --help    | -h
zvuk --version | -v`;

const transcode = `# Every .wav in raw/ becomes name.webm (Opus) + name.m4a (AAC) in public/sfx/
npx zvuk transcode "raw/*.wav" --out public/sfx

# Several folders keep their layout under --out (v2):
#   raw/sfx/hit.wav → public/audio/sfx/hit.webm
#   raw/ui/hit.wav  → public/audio/ui/hit.webm
npx zvuk transcode "raw/sfx/*.wav" "raw/ui/*.wav" --out public/audio

# Music at a higher bitrate, Opus only
npx zvuk transcode "music/*.wav" --out public/music --bitrate 128k --formats webm`;

const ffmpeg = `ffmpeg -y -i raw/coin.wav -c:a libopus -b:a 96k -vn public/sfx/coin.webm
ffmpeg -y -i raw/coin.wav -c:a aac     -b:a 96k -vn public/sfx/coin.m4a`;

const bank = `{
  "defaultBus": "sfx",
  "sounds": {
    "coin":  { "url": ["/sfx/coin.webm", "/sfx/coin.m4a"] },
    "spin":  { "url": ["/sfx/spin.webm", "/sfx/spin.m4a"], "loop": true },
    "theme": { "url": ["/music/theme.webm", "/music/theme.m4a"], "bus": "music" }
  }
}`;

const generated = `// AUTOGENERATED by \`zvuk gen\`. Do not edit.
import type { Engine, PreloadOptions } from '@schmooky/zvuk';

export type SoundName =
  | "coin"
  | "spin"
  | "theme";

export const BANK = [
  { name: "coin", url: ["/sfx/coin.webm","/sfx/coin.m4a"], bus: "sfx" },
  { name: "spin", url: ["/sfx/spin.webm","/sfx/spin.m4a"], bus: "sfx", loop: true },
  { name: "theme", url: ["/music/theme.webm","/music/theme.m4a"], bus: "music" },
] as const;

/** Load every sound in the bank. Rejects with PreloadError if any fail. */
export function loadBank(engine: Engine, options: PreloadOptions = {}): Promise<void> {
  return engine.preload(
    BANK.map((entry) => ({
      name: entry.name,
      url: entry.url,
      options: 'bus' in entry ? { bus: entry.bus as string } : {},
    })),
    options,
  );
}`;

const use = `import { BANK, loadBank, type SoundName } from './bank.gen';

// PreloadOptions: concurrency, progress, bytes, an abort signal.
await loadBank(engine, { concurrency: 4, onProgress: ({ completed, total }) => bar(completed / total) });

// loop is data on the entry, for the call site to honour.
function play(name: SoundName) {
  const entry = BANK.find((e) => e.name === name)!;
  return engine.sound(name).play({ loop: 'loop' in entry && entry.loop });
}

play('coin');  // ✓
play('cion');  // ✗ type error, caught before it becomes a SoundNotFoundError`;

const v1gen = `// v1 output                                   // v2 output
loadBank(engine, { normalize: true })           loadBank(engine, { concurrency, onProgress, signal })
  → Promise.all(engine.loadSound(...))            → engine.preload(...)  (PreloadError on failure)
{ name, url, options: { bus, loop: true } }     { name, url, bus, loop: true }
empty bank → invalid TypeScript                 empty bank → type SoundName = never
duplicate name → last one wins                  duplicate name → error`;
---
<Docs
  title="CLI"
  description="Two commands ship with the package. One transcodes a folder into the webm + m4a codec ladder, the other turns a sound manifest into a typed module."
  eyebrow="Reference"
>
  <p>
    The ffmpeg loop from the <a href="/guides/asset-formats/">asset formats</a>
    guide gets copy-pasted into every project's scripts folder, and so does a
    hand-maintained list of sound names that drifts from the files. The
    <code>zvuk</code> binary packages both.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is installed with the package as <code>zvuk</code> and runs on Node 20
    or later. Run it through <code>npx zvuk</code>, <code>pnpm exec zvuk</code>,
    or from a <code>package.json</code> script.
  </p>
  <Snippet code={usage} lang="sh" title="Usage" />

  <h2>zvuk transcode</h2>
  <p>
    Runs ffmpeg once per input and format. Each input <code>name.ext</code>
    produces <code>name.webm</code> (libopus) and <code>name.m4a</code> (AAC)
    in the output directory, which is created if missing. Existing outputs are
    overwritten.
  </p>
  <p>
    Since v2 <Since v="2.0" /> outputs keep their folder layout relative to
    the deepest folder all inputs share. In 1.x every output landed flat in
    <code>--out</code>, so <code>sfx/hit.wav</code> and
    <code>ui/hit.wav</code> both wrote <code>hit.webm</code> and the second
    won. Two inputs that would still write the same file now stop the run
    with an error. <code>--formats</code> with an unknown or empty list, and
    any unknown option, also fail up front instead of being ignored.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>&lt;glob&gt;</code></td><td></td><td>One or more input paths. A <code>*</code> in the last path segment matches files in that directory; there is no <code>**</code>. Quote it so the shell doesn't expand it first.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--out &lt;dir&gt;</code></td><td><code>dist</code></td><td>Output directory.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--bitrate &lt;rate&gt;</code></td><td><code>96k</code></td><td>Passed to ffmpeg as <code>-b:a</code> for both formats.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--formats &lt;list&gt;</code></td><td><code>webm,m4a</code></td><td>Comma-separated; <code>webm</code> and <code>m4a</code> are the only accepted values. Anything else, or an empty list, is an error.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <Snippet code={transcode} lang="sh" />
  <p>Per input, that is exactly these two ffmpeg calls:</p>
  <Snippet code={ffmpeg} lang="sh" />

  <div class="pitfall">
    <div class="pitfall-title">ffmpeg is not bundled.</div>
    The command spawns <code>ffmpeg</code> from your <code>PATH</code> and
    fails on the first file if it can't. An encode error stops the run with
    ffmpeg's exit code; files already written stay.
  </div>

  <h2>zvuk gen</h2>
  <p>
    Reads a JSON manifest and writes a TypeScript module with a
    <code>SoundName</code> union, a <code>BANK</code> array, and a
    <code>loadBank(engine, options)</code> that loads every entry through
    <a href="/guides/loading/"><code>engine.preload</code></a>, so it takes
    <code>PreloadOptions</code> (concurrency, progress, byte progress, an
    abort signal) and rejects with <code>PreloadError</code> after every
    entry has settled. <code>--out</code> sets the output path, default
    <code>bank.gen.ts</code> in the current directory.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>sounds</code> can be an object keyed by name, as below, or an array
    of entries that each carry a <code>name</code>. Each entry takes
    <code>url</code> (a string or a codec ladder), and optionally
    <code>bus</code> and <code>loop</code>. <code>defaultBus</code> applies to
    entries that don't name one. A name listed twice, an entry without a
    name or URL, or a manifest without <code>sounds</code> is an error.
  </p>
  <Snippet code={bank} lang="json" title="bank.json" />
  <Snippet code={`npx zvuk gen bank.json --out src/audio/bank.gen.ts`} lang="sh" />
  <Snippet code={generated} lang="ts" title="src/audio/bank.gen.ts" />
  <p>
    <code>loop</code> stays on each <code>BANK</code> entry as data, because
    it describes how a sound is meant to play and <code>loadSound</code> has
    no such option. An empty bank produces <code>type SoundName = never</code>.
    Commit the generated file, or regenerate it in a <code>prebuild</code>
    script so it can't drift.
  </p>
  <Snippet code={use} lang="ts" />

  <h3>What changed in the generated module <Since v="2.0" /></h3>
  <p>
    Code that only calls <code>loadBank(engine)</code> keeps working. Code
    that passed load options to it, or read <code>entry.options</code>, has
    to change.
  </p>
  <Snippet code={v1gen} lang="plaintext" title="v1 → v2" hideBadge />

  <h2>--version <Since v="2.0" /></h2>
  <p>
    <code>zvuk --version</code> (or <code>-v</code>) prints the installed
    package version. Useful in CI logs, where the question is usually which
    copy of the CLI ran.
  </p>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/guides/asset-formats/">Asset formats</a> explains why the ladder is webm first, m4a second.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/asset-resolution/">Asset resolution</a> covers loading the transcoded files from a manifest or cache.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/loading/">Loading sounds</a> has <code>preload</code>, the batched alternative to <code>loadBank</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
